  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 104.31 Stream restoration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 104.31 “Stream restoration” means the process of converting an unstable, altered, or degraded watercourse, including adjacent riparian zone and flood-prone areas, to a natural condition as previously found at the site or as found in reaches of the watercourse that have not been altered by human disturbances.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19; renumbered by #13945 (formerly Env-Wt 104.29)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt100.html"
